<%- include('../partials/header') %>
<div class="row justify-content-center">
  <div class="col-lg-9 col-xl-8 legal-page">
    <h1 class="h2 mb-1">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted small">Last updated: <%= lastUpdated %></p>
    <p>This policy explains how Nespresso Tracker collects, uses and shares your personal data, and what rights you have under the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR), the Data Protection Act 2018 and the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations (PECR).</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="who-we-are">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>Nespresso Tracker is run by <strong>Red Kite Development</strong>, which is the controller of your personal data. You can contact us about anything in this policy at <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a>. We have not appointed a Data Protection Officer.</p>
    <p>Nespresso Tracker is an independent project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Nestlé or Nespresso.</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="data-we-collect">2. What personal data we collect</h2>
    <h3 class="h6">Data you give us</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your name, email address, and a password (stored only as a one-way hash, never in plain text), and your chosen machine type.</li>
      <li><strong>Your pod list:</strong> the pods you add, with brand, intensity, flavour, score, tasting notes and date tried. Other users cannot see your list, but administrators of the service can view accounts and pods in order to manage it.</li>
      <li><strong>Messages to us:</strong> anything you send to <%= contactEmail %>.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="h6">Data we create or collect automatically</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account records:</strong> when your account was created, when you confirmed your email address, and when you last logged in.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical data and cookies needed to run the site:</strong> a login session and a security token (see our <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>), and your IP address, which is processed when your browser connects to our servers.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics data, only if you accept analytics cookies:</strong> online identifiers stored in cookies, pages viewed, the date and time of visits, how you arrived at the site, your browser, device and operating system, and your approximate location (derived from your IP address). Google Analytics does not log or store individual IP addresses.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="why-we-use-it">3. Why we use your data and our lawful basis</h2>
    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table class="table table-sm align-top">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Lawful basis (UK GDPR Article 6)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Creating and running your account, storing your pods, and sending the emails needed to confirm your address or reset your password</td><td>Account details, pod list, account records</td><td>Contract: it is necessary to provide the service you asked for (Article 6(1)(b))</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Keeping the service secure and preventing abuse, for example login rate limiting and session protection</td><td>Technical data, cookies needed to run the site, IP address</td><td>Legitimate interests in keeping the service and its users safe (Article 6(1)(f)). Cookies that are strictly necessary are exempt from consent under PECR regulation 6(4)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Understanding how the site is used so we can improve it</td><td>Analytics data</td><td><strong>Your consent</strong> (Article 6(1)(a)), which is also what PECR regulation 6 requires before we store or read analytics cookies on your device. We do nothing for this purpose unless you accept</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Remembering your cookie choice</td><td>Consent cookie</td><td>Strictly necessary to respect your choice (PECR regulation 6(4)); legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f))</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Responding to your messages and requests, and meeting legal obligations</td><td>Messages, account details</td><td>Legitimate interests in answering you (Article 6(1)(f)); legal obligation (Article 6(1)(c)) where the law requires us to keep or disclose something</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>We do not sell your personal data, use it for advertising, or make decisions about you by automated means that have legal or similarly significant effects.</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="analytics">4. Analytics cookies and Google</h2>
    <p>If you choose <strong>Accept analytics</strong>, we load Google's tag (a Google Tag Manager container containing Google Analytics 4) on your device. Google then sets cookies and collects the analytics data listed above. Google acts as our processor and handles this data under its data processing terms.</p>
    <p>If you do not accept, <strong>nothing from Google is loaded</strong>: your browser makes no connection to Google's analytics or tag servers and no analytics cookies are set. Choosing not to accept makes no difference to how you can use Nespresso Tracker.</p>
    <p>You can withdraw your consent at any time, as easily as you gave it, using <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer of any page or the controls on our <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>. When you withdraw, analytics stops straight away, we remove the Google cookies we can reach, and the page reloads without Google's tag. Withdrawing does not affect the lawfulness of any processing carried out before you withdrew.</p>
    <p>We use your answer for six months before asking you again, or sooner if this policy changes in a way that affects it.</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="sharing">5. Who we share your data with</h2>
    <p>We use the following service providers, who process data on our behalf and only on our instructions:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> (Google Ireland Limited and Google LLC): analytics, only if you consent.</li>
      <li><strong>MongoDB, Inc. (MongoDB Atlas):</strong> database hosting for account details and pod lists.</li>
      <li><strong>Render Services, Inc. (Render):</strong> hosting for the website, which handles your IP address and requests.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend:</strong> sending confirmation and password-reset emails, which means it handles your name and email address.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Content from other websites.</strong> To display the site, your browser also loads fonts from Google Fonts and a "Buy me a coffee" button from Buy Me a Coffee. These providers receive your IP address and basic browser information when the page loads, and handle it under their own privacy policies. We do not share your account or pod data with them.</p>
    <p>We may also disclose personal data if the law or a court requires it.</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="transfers">6. Transfers outside the UK</h2>
    <p>Some of the providers above are based in, or may process data in, the United States and other countries outside the UK. Where this happens we rely on a recognised safeguard: the UK Extension to the EU–US Data Privacy Framework (the "UK–US data bridge") for certified recipients, or the UK International Data Transfer Addendum to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses (or the UK International Data Transfer Agreement). You can ask us for more information about these safeguards using the contact details above.</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="retention">7. How long we keep your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account details and pods:</strong> until your account is deleted. Ask us to delete it at <%= contactEmail %> and we will remove your account and pods.</li>
      <li><strong>Login sessions:</strong> up to 7 days after your last activity.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics data in Google Analytics:</strong> up to 2 months, after which Google deletes it automatically. Aggregated reports that do not identify you may be kept longer.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics cookies:</strong> they expire after up to 2 years, or are removed when you withdraw consent.</li>
      <li><strong>Your cookie choice:</strong> six months.</li>
      <li><strong>Hosting and security logs:</strong> kept by our hosting provider for a limited period.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="your-rights">8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>be <strong>informed</strong> about how we use your data (this policy);</li>
      <li><strong>access</strong> the personal data we hold about you;</li>
      <li>have inaccurate data <strong>corrected</strong>;</li>
      <li>have your data <strong>erased</strong> in some circumstances;</li>
      <li><strong>restrict</strong> how we use your data in some circumstances;</li>
      <li><strong>data portability</strong>: receive the data you gave us in a portable format;</li>
      <li><strong>object</strong> to processing that relies on legitimate interests;</li>
      <li><strong>withdraw consent</strong> at any time (see section 4), and</li>
      <li>not be subject to decisions based solely on automated processing that have legal or similarly significant effects (we do not make any).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To use any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a>. We will reply within one month. We may need to confirm your identity first.</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="required">9. Do you have to give us your data?</h2>
    <p>You need to give us your name, email address and a password to create an account, because we cannot provide the service without them. Everything else is optional, and analytics cookies are entirely your choice.</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="complaints">10. Complaints</h2>
    <p>If you are unhappy with how we use your data, please tell us first so we can put it right. You also have the right to complain to the UK supervisory authority, the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO): <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a>, telephone 0303 123 1113.</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4" id="changes">11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We will update this policy when our use of your data changes and show the date at the top. If a change affects analytics cookies, we will ask for your choice again.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
